  "claim": "The king deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688 was supported by Nicholas Barnewall. He is the grandson of the man the Grace Dieu Abbey was acquired by in 1541.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: It was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall, who had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\nPage: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: His grandson, the third Viscount, was a supporter of James II and outlawed.\nPage: James II of England. Sentence: James II and VII (14 October 1633 – 16 September 1701) was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII, from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\nPage: Patrick Barnewall (Solicitor General). Sentence: He belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown: his own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.\nPage: Grace Dieu Abbey. Sentence: Nonetheless it was suppressed in 1541 and acquired by Patrick Barnewall.",
