        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e0cb7a31-fee4-59aa-8be6-a079ab60255b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Barnewall, Patrick Barnewall, James II and VII, the third Viscount Barnewall\n- Titles and families: Viscount Barnewall, Lord Trimlestown, Barnewall family\n- Places and organizations: County Dublin, Irish House of Commons, Grace Dieu Abbey\n- Events: suppression of Grace Dieu Abbey, creation of Viscount Barnewall, Glorious Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Grace Dieu Abbey was suppressed in 1541 and was acquired by Patrick Barnewall.\n- The title Viscount Barnewall was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall.\n- Nicholas Barnewall had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\n- James II and VII was born on 14 October 1633 and was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\n- The third Viscount Barnewall was a supporter of James II and was outlawed.\n- Patrick Barnewall, Solicitor General, belonged to a junior branch of the Lord Trimlestown family.\n- Patrick Barnewall's descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ace13245-f244-5f2c-afce-292efe405ff3",
        "text": "Page: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: It was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall, who had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\nPage: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: His grandson, the third Viscount, was a supporter of James II and outlawed.\nPage: James II of England. Sentence: James II and VII (14 October 1633 – 16 September 1701) was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII, from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\nPage: Patrick Barnewall (Solicitor General). Sentence: He belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown: his own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.\nPage: Grace Dieu Abbey. Sentence: Nonetheless it was suppressed in 1541 and acquired by Patrick Barnewall.",
